{{ spec.info.title }} tools for [Codex](https://github.com/openai/codex). This plugin packages {{ spec.info.title }} SDK skills, {{ spec.info.title }} deployment workflow skills, and the hosted {{ spec.info.title }} MCP server.

## Installation

### From the OpenAI Curated marketplace

1. Run `codex`, then run `/plugins`.
2. Switch to the **OpenAI Curated** marketplace.
3. Search for **{{ spec.info.title }}** and install the plugin.
4. Sign in to {{ spec.info.title }} and approve access when prompted, then start a new Codex session.

The plugin can also be installed from **Plugins** in the ChatGPT desktop app.

### From this repository

Add this repository as a marketplace and install the plugin from it:

```sh
codex plugin marketplace add {{ sdk.gitUserName }}/{{ sdk.gitRepoName }}
codex plugin add {{ name }}@{{ name }}
```

Start a new Codex session to load the bundled skills.

### Manual setup

To use the skills and the MCP server without the plugin, copy the skills into your user skills folder and register the server.

macOS / Linux:

```sh
mkdir -p ~/.agents/skills
cp -R plugins/{{ name }}/skills/* ~/.agents/skills/
codex mcp add {{ name }} --url https://mcp.appwrite.io/
```

Windows (PowerShell):

```powershell
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "$HOME\.agents\skills" | Out-Null
Copy-Item -Recurse plugins\{{ name }}\skills\* "$HOME\.agents\skills\"
codex mcp add {{ name }} --url https://mcp.appwrite.io/
```

Instead of `codex mcp add`, you can merge `plugins/{{ name }}/config.toml` into `~/.codex/config.toml`.

