The language skills give Codex language-specific {{ spec.info.title }} context for authentication, database queries, storage, realtime, functions, and server-side administration. The `deploy-site` and `deploy-function` skills walk through deploying {{ spec.info.title }} Sites and Functions with the {{ spec.info.title }} CLI.

Codex loads a skill when a task matches its `description`. To invoke one explicitly, type `$` or run `/skills` and pick it.

## Hosted MCP server

The plugin registers one `{{ name }}` server at `https://mcp.appwrite.io/`. It provides tools for working with your {{ spec.info.title }} organizations and projects, and for searching the latest {{ spec.info.title }} documentation.

The hosted server uses browser-based OAuth, so no API key, project ID, endpoint, or other manually configured secret is required. Codex asks you to sign in when you install the plugin. To sign in again, or after a manual setup, run:

```sh
codex mcp login {{ name }}
```

Then try:

> Use {{ spec.info.title }} to show my workspace context and list my projects.

If the browser does not open, use the authorization URL printed by Codex. Run `codex mcp logout {{ name }}` followed by `codex mcp login {{ name }}` to refresh the OAuth session, and `codex mcp list` to check that the server is configured.

